Z||000000||lildevil||08-25-2001||11:08 AM||||Went to Maryland International Raceway lastnite and was able to get 7 runs in.  Here are my runs in order with 60 foot times.  My best til last nite was a 13.311 @ 100.75 mph.<P>13.505 @ 99.17             1.882 60 foot<BR>13.432 @ 99.74             1.881<BR>13.414 @ 99.87             1.865<BR>**13.240 @ 101.24            1.870**<BR>**13.232 @ 100.32            1.819**<BR>14.443 @ 97.53             2.237<BR>13.306 @ 99.91             1.842<P>Runs 4 and 5 were my best ETS and mph to date. HEE YA!  Run 6 I spun tires all the way through first then the car shifted to third and i couldn't get iit to down shift.  The car next to me red lighted so i survived til the next round where i raced a Hyundai Accent all riced up.  This guy ran a 18.85 1/4 mile time!  And hes doing a burn out!  Well we get to the light and his side goes down to green.  Well i am sitting there and sitting there for 5 seconds!  It seemed like an eternity!  Well i think i was alsleep goes my reaction time sucked on that run and the hyundai beat me because he ran a 18.852 on a 18.84 dial in. Can't wait til it gets colder.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.311 @100.75 mph<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||08-25-2001||12:18 PM||||what did you ahve in for your dial time? <BR>i went to the track with my car.  its all stock and dial a 15.9 most of the time.  got to the 4th round and the guy next to me in a camero missed a shift.  but my dumba$$ kept goin all the way and clocked a 15.83 or something.  i was pissed.  oh well it was fun and i got to see what my car can do.  cant wait to go next summer.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000002||pontiacs4me||08-25-2001||01:59 PM||||Earl,<P>what transmission are you running with this setup?  Have you done any mods to the SC 3800?  Those 60 foots are awesome!||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||08-25-2001||04:05 PM||||Wow.   Awesome!  Those 60' especially, good 'ol mid-engine traction :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||banditbalz||08-25-2001||09:21 PM||||congrats! That's impressive considering we have a GTA member that has a s/c 3800 and a 20lb bottle of NOS connected to a 5 speed tranny and he has a best of 14.4. I guess some guys just know how to get their cars rolling....<P>Time to change your sig. <P>_<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2.jpg">  <P><BR>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!<p>[This message has been edited by banditbalz (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||1
