Z||000007||NOS3800||08-26-2001||12:36 AM||||I guess Immortal is a non beliver. We have the timeslips, and video! Anyway, I got my first side by side run against my brother (Lildv1l) the nite in this thread. He creamed me, but I had an empty bottle, it only had two pounds. Anyway, I ran 14.08 against his 13.43. Well I was pissed. I refilled the bottle at the track which I did not realize they did till late. Next run was MY fastest ever, a 13.45 at 99.70. 60' was an awesome (for me) 1.888. Now I need a purge valve, get those 60's even lower. I got another run in with tire spin. I got a 60' time of 1.939. I beat the other guy so bad I pushed the brakes and finished with a 13.73 at 81.87 mph. My final run in eliminations I FORGOT to turn my NOS back on after my burnout. I didn't turn it on till around 100 ft. Still ran a 14.39 at 98.69 mph. Can't wait to get my act together and really race my brother head to head.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||8
Z||000008||lildevil||08-26-2001||12:48 AM||||My car uses the 4t65e automatic. I added a 3.4 pulley which adds betwwen 25-30 HP. Not bad for 100 dollars.   I am using a reproggrammed PCM also which doesn't do much for 1/4 mile times but gets rid of the speedlimiter and changes the shift points slightly.  <P>Bandit, is the fellow your talking about have a 3.8 Series 1 or Series 2?  Theres a big difference in the horsepower. And if hes shooting NOS and its not tuned right it is probably counter productive. Also have him check his knock retard to see if its running right. <P>Phil... do you want to run your car for High Performance Magazine?  email me directly.  Trying to get something goin this year before it gets too cold.<P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero38SC||11-03-2001||10:47 PM||||Well, I got some new times to share.<P>1st run:<BR>14.785 @89.47 (things went wrong. see below)<P>2nd Run:<BR>13.160 @ 105.35 MPH (Come on lildevil  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>3rd Run:<BR>13.181 @ 103.47 MPH (Lots of Tire Spin)<P>4th Run:<BR>13.642 @ 101.02 MPH (Even more tire spin)<P>This is the first running with the new West Coast Clutch.  First run I bent my cradle where I have one of the motor mounts.  The engine torqued up and I broke one of the coil packs in half on the deck lid hinge.  I guess I hooked up really well off of the line!<P>2nd run I put in my spare coil pack and used cable ties to move it away for the danm hinge.  As you can see, I did much better.<P>3rd and 4th runs, I got put the tires up in smoke off of the line.  I have got to hook up better.  I launching just above idel and then punching it.  I either need to back off or get better tires.<P>Maybe next weekend at the Maryland track.  <P>Lildevil, do you have that info again?<P>Jason||||reg||1
