Z||000013||lildevil||11-05-2001||09:57 PM||||Well i am impressed with your times Jason. With some better tires you'll be in the 12's before you know it. i can't wait to get our cars side by side. I got my car to run a 13.21 on a  hot motor two weeks ago.  It wasn't that much of a difference then my last PB so i didn't post. But I swapped in a 3.25 pulley and reset the PCM after that run but it through everything out of wack after that. Man i wish i didn't do that. I got 13.5's and 13.6's after that.  But i figured out what to do so watch out this weekend.  I'll get that info for you tommorrow. The race is on Sunday from 10 til whenver i believe.  <P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||NOS3800||11-05-2001||10:45 PM||||Hey, what about me? I'll be there too. Jason, maybe you will actually get to see my car run below 14 seconds. Seems everytime you see me run I haven't run better then 14.0 for whatever reason. Last time at the track I ran a best 13.21 with some tire spin. I reworked the jets alittle more so I should be right with you as long as you don't run a 12! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||10
Z||000015||Wannabe||11-05-2001||11:42 PM||||For those of you up to adding more engine mods, have you heard of the high ration rockers that are available for the 3.8 SC? I'm partial to engines that pull at the top end, and according to the GTP guys, this mod dramatically improves power beyond 4500.||||reg||1
